        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Update `AuthenticatorAttestationResponse.getPublicKey()` support status for Safari]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29458</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29458"/>
        <updated>2026-04-12T23:41:37.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80624252?u=abb5f45720c0c7db48614fa1cfe4ed7032af0a36&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Sets Safari's support for <code class="notranslate">AuthenticatorAttestationResponse.getPublicKey()</code> to <code class="notranslate">partial</code>. The <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-3/#sctn-public-key-easy" rel="nofollow">Web Authentication API specification</a> (since level 2 where it was first described in) states that user agents MUST support algorithm -7 (ES256), -8 (Ed25519), and -257 (RS256). However, WebKit only supports -7 (ES256) and returns <code class="notranslate">null</code> for the other 2 algorithms.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/52dbebe20b922cab89928085f9dcfa8082a813e4/Source/WebCore/Modules/webauthn/AuthenticatorAttestationResponse.cpp#L162">WebKit source code</a></li>
<li>Tested on Safari 18.6 on macOS.</li>
</ul>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>pilcrowonpaper</name>
            <email>pilcrowonpaper@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/pilcrowonpaper</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2026-04-12T23:40:59.000Z</published>
    </entry>
